1
00:00:01,033 --> 00:00:02,100
<i>Did you give the flash drive
to the police?</i>

2
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:05,633
<i>I'm sure that woman
and her friends killed Ramon.</i>

3
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:09,133
<i>Just promise me that no one
will find out about this.</i>

4
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:10,733
<i> But it's broken.</i>

5
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:13,633
<i>I have someone I can go
to restore it.</i>

6
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:15,500
<i>Once you fix that,
there's more to come.</i>

7
00:00:15,633 --> 00:00:17,067
<i> Your father was worried</i>

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,267
<i>because he thought our enemies
were conspiring with the police.</i>

9
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,967
<i> Don't worry about us anymore.</i>

10
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,500
<i>Just don't come running to me
asking for my help.</i>

11
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:25,633
<i> When the truth comes out,</i>

12
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:27,867
<i>everyone will know
that father got setup.</i>

13
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:31,000
<i>Maybe Golda was just
an accomplice.</i>

14
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:32,200
<i> This is a surprise inspection!</i>

15
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:34,467
<i> If I kill Delgado now,</i>

16
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:36,767
<i>what, there will be another
investigation?</i>

17
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,700
<i>Especially since it's inside
the precinct!</i>

18
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:40,200
<i> There's evidence against you.</i>

19
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:42,167
<i>That's not mine. It was a setup.</i>

20
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,300
<i> Why are you hiding this?</i>

21
00:00:43,433 --> 00:00:45,667
<i>That's the only way I can
find out who did this.</i>

22
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,400
<i> Diego is Parak.</i>

23
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:49,233
<i>But he's the one the notebook
is pointing to.</i>

24
00:00:49,367 --> 00:00:53,000
<i>"Bulalakaw," that's the firing
range where Diego and I go.</i>

25
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:55,200
<i>And the gun that was found
in my car,</i>

26
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,733
<i> he could have planted it.</i>

27
00:00:56,867 --> 00:00:58,433
<i> Just follow the orders,</i>

28
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:00,733
<i>otherwise, Berdugo
will kill you.</i>

29
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:02,700
<i> Stop calling your godfather.</i>

30
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,533
<i> Maybe he's working.</i>

31
00:01:04,667 --> 00:01:07,467
<i>I just want to get an update
about that flash drive.</i>

32
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:33,300
Arms, please.

33
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,433
Sir, frisking.

34
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,300
Sir, clear!

35
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:51,567
I granted your request,
but don't break my trust.

36
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:52,967
Thank you, Chief.

37
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:04,133
Why do we have to talk here?

38
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,700
Why do you seem nervous?

39
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,233
What's that for?

40
00:02:36,367 --> 00:02:37,867
For your protection here.

41
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,467
Hide it.

42
00:02:43,567 --> 00:02:44,933
Protection?

43
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:45,933
Yes.

44
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,900
Who's going to kill me?

45
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,233
I was thinking,
you're going to do it, Diego.

46
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,100
Thank you.

47
00:02:58,833 --> 00:02:59,733
Hon...

48
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,433
- Hi, Hon. How was your workout?
- Okay.

49
00:03:03,567 --> 00:03:05,000
Is there any bad news?

50
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:06,700
Nothing.

51
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:08,333
Yvette.

52
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,900
You're so fast.

53
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:12,700
Is there a problem?

54
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:16,133
Actually, I have good news
for you.

55
00:03:16,267 --> 00:03:18,033
Mommy's medicine seems
to be effective

56
00:03:18,167 --> 00:03:20,333
because she's in a good mood
now.

57
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,267
That's great, I guess.

58
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,333
Yeah.

59
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:26,233
It's a good thing that
I'm just around the area.

60
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:27,633
You were in Bolagos?

61
00:03:28,367 --> 00:03:29,200
Where?

62
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:31,033
At the precinct.

63
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,167
What are you doing there?

64
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:35,500
Talking to Delgado.

65
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:38,033
But why?

66
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:46,133
I don't need that.

67
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,900
Please, Miguel.

68
00:03:50,267 --> 00:03:51,900
Don't joke like that.

69
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:54,867
What? Don't you want it?

70
00:03:55,867 --> 00:03:57,367
You know, it's risky.

71
00:03:58,667 --> 00:04:00,300
I might get in trouble
with that.

72
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:03,967
Like what happened to my car,

73
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,367
where they found a gun.

74
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:10,900
You know, Buddy,
only you can do that.

75
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:13,600
Do you know what you're saying,
Miguel?

76
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:17,067
Can you hear yourself now, Dude?

77
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:19,100
Yes.

78
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:22,400
I've noticed the change in you.

79
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,267
The way you dress,

80
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:26,367
your watch,

81
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,600
and your car.

82
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:31,633
You're such a big shot now,
Diego.

83
00:04:33,133 --> 00:04:34,900
Who pays you now?

84
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,500
Are you also a puppet
of the syndicates?

85
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:43,433
I was hoping Delgado
would talk, and finally,

86
00:04:43,567 --> 00:04:45,267
get a confession out of him...

87
00:04:45,867 --> 00:04:46,833
but he didn't.

88
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:49,433
He's still playing hard to get.

89
00:04:51,467 --> 00:04:55,800
Given the depth of Delgado's
involvement, he wouldn't talk.

90
00:04:56,833 --> 00:04:59,733
And remember, he's a cop.

91
00:04:59,867 --> 00:05:01,567
He knows all the tricks.

92
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:04,667
Maybe.

93
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,500
If I were you,

94
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:10,067
I'd focus on something else.

95
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,633
Delgado's case is old news.

96
00:05:12,767 --> 00:05:14,900
Don't waste your time on him.

97
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:17,167
He's in jail.

98
00:05:17,733 --> 00:05:19,033
His story is over.

99
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:20,500
Let's see.

100
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:23,700
Anyway, I'll talk to mom.

101
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:24,867
Okay.

102
00:05:28,233 --> 00:05:30,700
Why do you look at me like
that now, Miguel?

103
00:05:31,967 --> 00:05:34,133
We've been together
for a long time, Buddy.

104
00:05:35,767 --> 00:05:37,333
What? Because of the one who's
helping you from the outside?

105
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:38,267
Who?

106
00:05:38,933 --> 00:05:40,200
That Golda?

107
00:05:41,767 --> 00:05:44,800
Miguel, are you going
to believe her more than me?

108
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:47,267
Well, she's just lying.

109
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,167
You talk as if you know Golda
very well.

110
00:05:52,033 --> 00:05:53,367
Be honest with me.

111
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,667
Are you a true friend?

112
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,767
Tell me the truth.

113
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:07,967
I reminded Parak of your order
to kill Delgado.

114
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,533
Good.

115
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,833
He seemed to object.

116
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,033
It seems he didn't want
to do it.

117
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:20,900
But I reminded him that he would
be dead if he didn't do it.

118
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
I know he will.

119
00:06:25,867 --> 00:06:27,367
I trust Diego.

120
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,367
He's never let us down.

121
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:40,467
What?

122
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,200
Are you going to kill me?

123
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,233
Go ahead.

124
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:47,633
Prove to me that you're
a useless cop

125
00:06:48,467 --> 00:06:50,333
and a useless friend.

126
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:52,600
Miguel...

127
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,533
I've done everything
I can to protect you.

128
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:02,067
Now, if you don't want to accept
this help I'm giving you,

129
00:07:02,767 --> 00:07:04,667
there's nothing I can do,
Miguel.

130
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:07,433
Remember, I warned you.

131
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,733
Be careful here.

132
00:07:18,533 --> 00:07:20,233
It's you who should be careful.

133
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:23,800
If it's the devil
you're serving,

134
00:07:23,933 --> 00:07:26,400
they'll drag you to hell too.

135
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,400
Joey.

136
00:07:48,567 --> 00:07:49,200
Your phone.

137
00:07:49,333 --> 00:07:50,867
You might forget it.

138
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,800
Thank you.

139
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:55,800
I just really want to talk
to godfather in person

140
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,100
about the flash drive.

141
00:07:58,700 --> 00:07:59,500
Hey.

142
00:07:59,633 --> 00:08:00,533
You ready?

143
00:08:02,367 --> 00:08:03,533
Ready for what?

144
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:05,333
I'm going with you.

145
00:08:06,533 --> 00:08:07,700
I'm your bodyguard.

146
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,533
I'll go where you go.

147
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,267
Jin Ho, no need.

148
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,533
I insist.

149
00:08:13,267 --> 00:08:14,767
Somebody might attack you.

150
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,200
I have to be there.

151
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:18,933
Okay, fine.

152
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:22,133
In that case, I'll go too!

153
00:08:22,467 --> 00:08:23,933
I will join too.

154
00:08:24,267 --> 00:08:25,033
No need.

155
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:27,233
I can protect Joey on my own.

156
00:08:27,367 --> 00:08:30,067
If you insist, I insist too.

157
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:32,967
Hey, you'll just get in the way,
Peter.

158
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,333
Just stay here.

159
00:08:35,467 --> 00:08:37,700
Joey trusts me more than you,
right?

160
00:08:37,833 --> 00:08:38,733
So just take me with you.

161
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:40,400
- Not him.
- It's not about the trust.

162
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,633
I'm more skilled than you are.

163
00:08:43,267 --> 00:08:45,000
Can you guys please stop?

164
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,467
I've fixed it, Sir.

165
00:08:47,267 --> 00:08:48,633
I've retrieved it.

166
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:50,100
Okay, okay.

167
00:08:51,667 --> 00:08:52,633
Here, Sir.

168
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,533
There's just one video, Sir.

169
00:08:56,667 --> 00:08:58,533
That's fine. Watch it first.

170
00:09:08,767 --> 00:09:10,567
What are we going to do here,
Sir?

171
00:09:11,733 --> 00:09:14,267
Well, transfer it to a new
flash drive first,

172
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:16,967
and then throw away the old one,
okay?

173
00:09:17,267 --> 00:09:17,867
Okay.

174
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,500
Okay, okay.

175
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,933
Better yet, I'll just call
godfather.

176
00:09:39,567 --> 00:09:41,333
Hey, do that later.

177
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:42,867
You can do that later.

178
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,100
- Have a snack first. Go ahead.
- Okay, Sir.

179
00:09:49,233 --> 00:09:50,300
Hello?

180
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,333
Joey...

181
00:09:51,767 --> 00:09:52,500
Hello, Godfather.

182
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:54,000
<i> I'm sorry.</i>

183
00:09:54,133 --> 00:09:56,900
I was planning to call you,
you just beat me to it.

184
00:09:57,233 --> 00:10:01,467
Regarding the flash drive
you gave me,

185
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:03,267
I was going to let you know.

186
00:10:03,667 --> 00:10:04,867
How was it?

187
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:06,933
Has the flash drive
been restored?

188
00:10:08,933 --> 00:10:09,900
No, my child.

189
00:10:10,367 --> 00:10:12,667
I've been to three experts.

190
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,533
<i>They really can't restore
the flash drive.</i>

191
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:17,333
They said the damage
is too much.

192
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,100
I'm sorry, Joey.

193
00:10:19,233 --> 00:10:20,267
<i> Is that so?</i>

194
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,833
Okay. Thank you for trying,
Godfather.

195
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:24,933
But, Joey...

196
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:31,900
remember, it's not because
we didn't do anything today,

197
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,000
you're going to get discouraged.

198
00:10:35,533 --> 00:10:39,600
We can't control everything.

199
00:10:40,267 --> 00:10:41,267
Okay.

200
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:43,600
Thank you anyway.

201
00:10:45,967 --> 00:10:47,233
Bye, Godfather.

202
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:05,967
Hey, customer,
buy some empanadas.

203
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,767
Give me a dozen, hurry.

204
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:10,533
I'm sorry.

205
00:11:10,667 --> 00:11:11,900
I'll just buy two pieces.

206
00:11:12,033 --> 00:11:14,333
My husband and daughter
are not living with me anymore.

207
00:11:14,467 --> 00:11:15,833
You only bought two pieces.

208
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:18,233
Yes, because it's just me
in my house.

209
00:11:18,367 --> 00:11:19,333
- Here you go.
- Oh, right.

210
00:11:19,467 --> 00:11:20,667
Okay. Where are you going now?

211
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,533
To the market to shop.

212
00:11:22,667 --> 00:11:25,300
- Thank you. Take care.
- Thank you. See you tomorrow!

213
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:28,900
Miss, what's happening?

214
00:11:29,033 --> 00:11:30,767
There's a feeding program there,
Ma'am.

215
00:11:31,567 --> 00:11:33,233
- Okay, thank you.
- Okay.

216
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,233
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

217
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:42,300
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

218
00:11:42,467 --> 00:11:44,267
Don't be shy. Just eat.

219
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:47,000
Thank you.

220
00:12:01,367 --> 00:12:03,500
Miss, here's some food.

221
00:12:05,167 --> 00:12:06,800
Where's my comb?

222
00:12:07,833 --> 00:12:09,067
Who took my comb?

223
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,833
- You must be the one, right?
- Oh, no, not me.

224
00:12:10,967 --> 00:12:12,400
You took my comb!

225
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:13,700
No, Miss. Just calm down.

226
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:16,767
Miss, give me back my comb.
Give me back my comb!

227
00:12:16,933 --> 00:12:18,267
- No.
- Give me back my comb!

228
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,367
- It's not me.
- Give me back my comb!

229
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:24,167
- Wait, wait...
- Thieves!

230
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,467
- I'll borrow this first.
- Give me back my comb!

231
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,200
- Let me take care of this.
- You're all thieves!

232
00:12:29,333 --> 00:12:31,367
- Thieves!
- No, let me do it.

233
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,367
- My comb!
- Miss...

234
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,267
Miss, it's okay.

235
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,500
We'll find your comb.

236
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,400
Let's find your comb.

237
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:43,033
- My comb.
- Sit down first.

238
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:45,867
We will find your comb.

239
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,433
- Promise?
- Hush now. Yes, yes.

240
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:53,633
What now? How can we help
father now?

241
00:12:55,267 --> 00:12:57,167
I just want to get our problem
solved

242
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,833
so we can be complete again.

243
00:12:59,967 --> 00:13:01,900
But what are we going to do?

244
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:06,067
Maybe...

245
00:13:06,933 --> 00:13:09,100
there's something I can do
to help.

246
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:14,433
Hey, the best thing that you
can do is to catch Theresa.

247
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,633
Find a way to make her confess
to the police!

248
00:13:17,767 --> 00:13:20,467
But the only lead that I have
is Joey's video.

249
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,067
This guy is useless.

250
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,500
What kind of an agent are you?

251
00:13:25,633 --> 00:13:28,033
You're useless!
You're worthless!

252
00:13:28,267 --> 00:13:29,633
Then what do you call yourself?

253
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,033
You can't even do anything.

254
00:13:31,167 --> 00:13:32,133
Yeah.

255
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:34,467
But you're the expert here,
not me!

256
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,167
And you can't even help Joey!

257
00:13:44,367 --> 00:13:45,400
Sorry.

258
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:49,267
Oh, my, Ma'am, you have a wound.

259
00:13:52,967 --> 00:13:54,567
Do you have a first aid kit?

260
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,300
Do you have a first aid kit?

261
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,933
Ma'am, sit down here.

262
00:14:04,067 --> 00:14:05,167
Thank you.

263
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,567
Thank you.

264
00:14:14,167 --> 00:14:15,633
Just a moment.

265
00:14:23,567 --> 00:14:25,233
Just a moment.

266
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,700
Why is Delgado still alive?

267
00:14:31,467 --> 00:14:33,833
And lately, we've been having a
hard time contacting you, Parak.

268
00:14:35,133 --> 00:14:39,133
I've just been busy, but I've
fixed the hit for Delgado.

269
00:14:39,267 --> 00:14:41,767
I've already spoken to someone
who will do that.

270
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,300
Are you sure?

271
00:14:45,933 --> 00:14:48,267
Maybe it'll take another week.

272
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:53,433
Berdugo is growing impatient.

273
00:14:53,833 --> 00:14:54,867
I know. Why?

274
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,533
Who said I wouldn't do what
you're asking me to do?

275
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:59,500
Didn't I say I would?

276
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,033
So stop nagging me!

277
00:15:14,467 --> 00:15:16,833
You know, I'm starting to doubt
Parak's actions.

278
00:15:18,367 --> 00:15:19,733
Oh, come on.

279
00:15:20,033 --> 00:15:21,500
You're just jealous.

280
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,333
What?

281
00:15:23,467 --> 00:15:25,233
Why would I be jealous?

282
00:15:25,867 --> 00:15:27,933
Because you know that there
is a possibility

283
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:30,767
that Parak will take your
position from Berdugo,

284
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:32,933
as well as here in our group.

285
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,767
That won't happen,

286
00:15:36,533 --> 00:15:38,733
especially since Parak seems
to be hiding something.

287
00:15:40,367 --> 00:15:41,767
I'll take care of him.

288
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,133
There you go, it's done.

289
00:15:53,867 --> 00:15:54,867
Thank you.

290
00:15:55,833 --> 00:15:57,100
Clarissa.

291
00:15:58,367 --> 00:15:59,867
Clarissa.

292
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,567
I'm Yvette.

293
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,833
Hello.

294
00:16:02,967 --> 00:16:05,433
Thank you for what you did
earlier.

295
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:10,267
Not what you did to me,
not that.

296
00:16:10,433 --> 00:16:13,567
But what you did to that woman.

297
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,300
Where did you learn that?

298
00:16:15,733 --> 00:16:19,967
I trained in the psych ward
as a nurse.

299
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:22,100
But I didn't push through
with it

300
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:24,433
because I got married
and had a child.

301
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:26,767
That's why I focused
on my family.

302
00:16:27,267 --> 00:16:29,033
Too bad.

303
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:30,800
You're so skilled.

304
00:16:31,967 --> 00:16:37,400
But, well, being a full-time
housewife is also fulfilling.

305
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:42,833
Yes, but now, my husband
and daughter are busy,

306
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,667
so I'm home alone.

307
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:46,433
It's sad too.

308
00:16:48,333 --> 00:16:50,767
Do you want to be busy again?

309
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:56,200
You know, we have an upcoming
medical mission

310
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:58,133
at our foundation.

311
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:00,933
You might want to practice
what you've learned again.

312
00:17:01,067 --> 00:17:03,033
We need more volunteers.

313
00:17:03,533 --> 00:17:08,933
And you'll learn a lot at our
foundation if you join us.

314
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,367
What? Are you up for it?

315
00:17:17,133 --> 00:17:18,933
Aida, Aida...

316
00:17:19,233 --> 00:17:20,500
Give me a brochure.

317
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,200
There, here you go.

318
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:27,600
Read it.

319
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:29,367
Okay.

320
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:30,700
Think about it.

321
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,667
I can't believe
I'm moving again.

322
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:44,833
It's up to you!

323
00:17:44,967 --> 00:17:46,500
If you like to stay
in that place

324
00:17:46,633 --> 00:17:49,767
where there's leaking water
from the ceiling, then go!

325
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:51,900
So I don't have to share a room
with anyone!

326
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:54,267
Joey...

327
00:17:55,367 --> 00:17:56,533
are you okay?

328
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:01,500
You know it's a good thing
that grandmother

329
00:18:01,767 --> 00:18:03,833
has another boarding house,
right?

330
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,300
So we can at least be
comfortable

331
00:18:06,433 --> 00:18:08,500
while the other one is being
renovated, right?

332
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:25,300
So, Mom...

333
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:28,233
How do you feel
about your new meds?

334
00:18:29,933 --> 00:18:34,133
I feel much, much better
than I have in months.

335
00:18:34,267 --> 00:18:37,000
They said my meds are new.

336
00:18:37,133 --> 00:18:39,433
So, I like it.

337
00:18:40,633 --> 00:18:42,267
I see that, actually.

338
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,867
- Really?
- Yeah. I see that you're...

339
00:18:45,167 --> 00:18:46,600
Careful.

340
00:18:46,867 --> 00:18:49,233
I see that you're happier.

341
00:18:50,967 --> 00:18:57,700
Hopefully, happy enough
to give your son some advice?

342
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:01,167
Okay.

343
00:19:02,667 --> 00:19:03,867
Speak up.

344
00:19:05,267 --> 00:19:06,267
Okay.

345
00:19:08,733 --> 00:19:12,233
How can you earn someone's
trust?

346
00:19:18,467 --> 00:19:21,833
First question,
are you still a villain?

347
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:25,900
What do you mean, Mom?

348
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:31,133
Because when you were young,
you were always contradicting.

349
00:19:32,033 --> 00:19:34,333
You always wanted to be right.

350
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:38,267
Now, my question is...

351
00:19:40,767 --> 00:19:49,000
would you trust someone
if they always oppose you?

352
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,333
Well...

353
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:54,367
it depends.

354
00:19:54,833 --> 00:20:00,133
How can someone trust you
if you don't correct them?

355
00:20:02,533 --> 00:20:06,633
Trust is based on truth, right?

356
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:12,600
Trust is based on feelings.

357
00:20:14,567 --> 00:20:16,067
Yes, Andrew.

358
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:23,733
You have to win someone's heart
first to make them trust you.

359
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:30,467
You have to win their heart,
and not always contradict them.

360
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,167
When you win their trust,

361
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:36,833
that's when you make them
see your truth.

362
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:47,100
How are we going
to be together again?

363
00:20:49,233 --> 00:20:51,567
I miss us being complete.

364
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:05,667
<i> Father, I'll give you this!</i>

365
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,967
<i>This is the evidence
that will clear your name!</i>

366
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:10,733
<i>Wait a minute! It's really here!</i>

367
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:12,167
<i> Where is it?</i>

368
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:15,600
<i>I have evidence!
You can't take my father!</i>

369
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,100
<i> Is he really a hero,</i>

370
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:19,700
<i>or is he also a member
of the syndicate?</i>

371
00:21:21,567 --> 00:21:22,567
It's Golda...

372
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,367
<i>Did you write this?
I don't understand.</i>

373
00:21:42,533 --> 00:21:43,933
<i> What does that mean?</i>

374
00:21:46,767 --> 00:21:47,767
Joey, Joey!

375
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:48,933
Joey!

376
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,967
We will take care of your stuff
from the other dorm.

377
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:53,833
Oppa and I will carry
your things.

378
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:56,767
We will?

379
00:21:58,033 --> 00:21:58,800
Yes.

380
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,533
Okay.

381
00:22:01,667 --> 00:22:03,400
I'll just get food
for all of us.

382
00:22:03,533 --> 00:22:05,267
- I'll go outside.
- I'll come with you.

383
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,433
Let's go eat.

384
00:22:06,667 --> 00:22:07,800
Me too!

385
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:10,800
We'll finish the transfer later.
Let's eat first.

386
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:17,067
Okay, but can you change first?
Wear something presentable.

387
00:22:19,367 --> 00:22:22,767
And, I want to try a new place,
but it's a bit far from here.

388
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:25,000
Can we use your car?

389
00:22:25,633 --> 00:22:27,867
It's good that you agreed
to let us come with you.

390
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,900
I'm thinking of taking it back.
You're so slow.

391
00:22:32,033 --> 00:22:35,467
Get dressed, and get your keys.
Hurry up!

392
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,800
- Okay, just wait.
- Okay, I will change.

393
00:22:37,933 --> 00:22:39,133
Jin Ho, get your car.

394
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,133
Andrew?

395
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,100
Andrew!

396
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:08,733
Andrew!

397
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:11,567
JoeyOnDuty?

398
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:14,933
What are you doing here?

399
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:17,567
Boss Budol...

400
00:23:18,333 --> 00:23:19,567
I mean, Andrew.

401
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:24,233
I know...

402
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:28,133
you told me to stay away
from you...

403
00:23:29,467 --> 00:23:31,433
and I said a lot of unkind
things to you,

404
00:23:31,567 --> 00:23:34,333
besides telling you
to leave me alone.

405
00:23:36,833 --> 00:23:39,400
But I need your help.

406
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:42,467
Help for what?

407
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:46,300
I need to find Golda.

408
00:23:58,667 --> 00:24:00,867
What if he doesn't want to do
what you're making him do?

409
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:03,367
That's the payment for the sins
I've committed against you.

410
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:06,033
I did everything to protect
your husband.

411
00:24:06,167 --> 00:24:08,400
Parak can't fight the group.

412
00:24:08,533 --> 00:24:10,067
He knows better than
to fight us.

413
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:14,367
I know why Parak can't seem
to eliminate Delgado.

414
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:15,500
We're looking for Joey.

415
00:24:15,633 --> 00:24:16,733
She left a while ago.

416
00:24:16,867 --> 00:24:19,300
Maybe she just wants
to leave alone.

417
00:24:19,433 --> 00:24:22,400
I asked Andrew
to help me find Golda.

418
00:24:22,533 --> 00:24:23,800
Why doesn't she seem to be
coming back?

419
00:24:23,933 --> 00:24:24,833
Looks like someone's
already there.

420
00:24:24,967 --> 00:24:26,067
I think Golda's there.

421
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,367
Your happy days are over, Parak.

422
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,367
This is what he's using.

423
00:24:30,533 --> 00:24:31,533
Do you know him, Father?

424
00:24:31,667 --> 00:24:32,733
Who?
